---
// Goal: show that a test replays saved answers with no API key and no
// network, and that a missing answer fails instead of sending.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import { CACHING_SEE } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { RECORDING_SEE } from '../../data/reference.mjs';
import { run } from '../../data/samples.mjs';

const shown = (page, name, see) => ({ ...run(page, name), see: see[name] });
const replay = shown('start/caching', '1-replay', CACHING_SEE);
const miss = shown('start/answer-cache', '3-miss', RECORDING_SEE);
const facts = shown('start/answer-cache', '4-facts', RECORDING_SEE);
const spec = (name, anchor = '') => `https://github.com/botassembly/thinkthen/blob/main/specification/${name}.md${anchor}`;

const MODES = [
  ['`--replay DIR`', 'yes', 'nothing; a miss exits 5', 'no'],
  ['`--record DIR`', 'no', 'every question', 'if storage is permitted, replacing a held answer'],
  ['`--cache DIR`, `THINKTHEN_CACHE`, or the default cache', 'yes', 'the questions it misses', 'if storage is permitted'],
  ['a cache with `--refresh-cache`, or the model `jev-latest`', 'no', 'every question', 'if storage is permitted, replacing a held answer'],
  ['`--no-cache`', 'no', 'every question', 'no'],
];
---
<Base title="Replay in tests" description="Replay saved answers in a test with no API key and no network. A missing answer fails instead of sending.">
  <h1>Replay in tests</h1>
  <p class="lede">Save the model's answers once. Every later test replays them with no API key and no network. A replay costs nothing and gives the same answer every time.</p>

  <h2 id="replay-in-a-test">Replay in a test</h2>
  <p>A folder of saved answers can sit beside your tests. <code>--replay</code> reads that folder alone. Every run on this page replays one small folder.</p>
  <Terminal run={replay} caption={replay.see} />
  <p>A run with <code>--record DIR</code> and an API key saves the folder. The answer cache holds the same rows, in <code>thinkthen.sqlite</code>. A folder committed for replay keeps them in <code>thinkthen.jsonl</code>. A saved answer holds the question and the reply's answer, never a header. No API key can reach it.</p>

  <h2 id="a-replay-miss">A missing answer fails</h2>
  <p>A replay never sends. A question the folder lacks stops the run with exit 5, and the message names its question key. Change the test to a question the folder holds, or save the new answer with a run that has an API key.</p>
  <Terminal run={miss} caption={miss.see} />

  <h2 id="facts">Prove that nothing was sent</h2>
  <p><code>--facts</code> prints one line of run facts last on standard error. It counts the records finished, the requests sent and the retries. It adds token counts when every live reply reported them. <code>cache_answers</code> counts answers from the answer cache, never from a replay or record folder. <code>seconds</code>, <code>call_id</code> and <code>command_ms</code> change on every run. This example drops them.</p>
  <Terminal run={facts} caption={facts.see} />

  <h2 id="modes">The modes</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Looks up</th><th>Sends</th><th>Saves</th></tr>
    {MODES.map(([mode, look, send, save]) => (
      <tr><td>{mode.split('`').map((part, i) => (i % 2 ? <code>{part}</code> : part))}</td><td>{look}</td><td>{send}</td><td>{save}</td></tr>
    ))}
  </table>
  <p><code>--record</code> sends every question, even one the folder already holds, and may charge for it again. Use <code>--cache DIR</code> to reuse what a folder holds. An explicit <code>--record</code> or <code>--replay</code> replaces the default cache for that run. The <a href={spec('recording', '#the-options')}>recording specification</a> holds the full table.</p>

  <h2 id="elsewhere">Moved from this page</h2>
  <ul>
    <li id="plan"><a href="/start/plan/">See before you send</a> covers <code>--plan</code>.</li>
    <li id="the-key"><a href="/start/pay-once/#the-key">Pay once</a> says what makes two questions the same.</li>
    <li id="batching"><a href="/start/pay-once/#batching">Pay once</a> covers batching.</li>
    <li id="the-answer-cache"><a href="/start/configuration/#the-answer-cache">Configuration</a> covers the answer cache and storage rules.</li>
    <li id="pruning"><a href="/start/configuration/#pruning">Configuration</a> covers unused answers and pruning.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/start/pay-once/">Pay once</a> · <a href={spec('recording')}>The recording specification</a> · <a href="/learn/answers/#exit-codes">Every exit code</a></p>
</Base>
